w-it-all attitude could be problematic. Candidate A has quick decision making and calmness, but egocentric and poor communication, and unwillingness to further education.\n\nWe might argue that overall, Candidate D's problem solving and responsibility outweigh his temper? Or maybe Candidate C's technical competence is crucial for long-distance flights, and his leadership could mitigate his show-off attitude? Need to decide.\n\nGiven the panel hasn't fully discussed all criteria, we could ask a question to Agent 1 about Candidate B's memory for numbers impact on attention/accuracy. Or ask Agent 1 about any observed crew cooperation incidents for B. But we can also just make a contribution.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 3's recommendation. We can say: I see the strengths of B, but I am concerned about his memory for numbers and nasty remarks, which could affect safety. I think Candidate C's technical foresight may be more critical for long-distance flights, and his leadership could offset his show-off attitude if we provide feedback. So I might shift vote to C.\n\nBut we need to be careful: we must not introduce new facts not in our notes. We have all facts. So we can argue.\n\nLet's propose: I am less convinced by B due to communication and memory issues, and I think C's ability to anticipate dangerous situations and see complex connections is vital for long-haul flights, and his leadership is strong. While he is a show-off and not open to new ideas, those can be mitigated with training. So I vote for Candidate C.\n\nThus we need to state vote C.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 3's point. Provide evidence: B's weak memory for numbers, nasty remarks. Provide C's strengths: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership. Also note concerns: show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nExplain why C outweighs B: technical foresight and leadership are critical for long-distance, and B's communication issues could be more detrimental.\n\nThus final.\n\nWe need to output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
